 ('What is the Display → Diagnose → Decide approach?','Show what changed, investigate contributing drivers, then propose a responsible next step based on evidence.','It is a communication structure rather than proof that a driver caused the outcome. Keep observations, hypotheses and actions distinct.','Display lower monthly sales; diagnose by country/product/channel; decide which driver to validate with the owner.','Do not jump from one chart to an unverified root cause.','What evidence would you require before recommending a pricing change?','Beginner','concept',''),
 ('What should you say if asked for the business impact of a portfolio project built with synthetic data?','State that the result demonstrates the analytical workflow, not a measured real-world business impact.','You can discuss usability, data checks, repeatability and the decisions the prototype is designed to support. Do not claim cost savings or revenue increases without real evidence.','“The project shows how I would identify reporting questions and validate a metric. It does not claim real company savings because the sample data is synthetic.”','Do not invent percentage improvements to make a project sound stronger.','What measurable project-quality checks can you report instead?','Beginner','resume-integrity',''),
 ('How would you explain your personal contribution to a group or portfolio project?','Separate work you actually performed from templates, guidance, collaborators or planned work.','A clear boundary builds credibility. Be ready to explain your specific code, query, model or validation decision.','“I wrote the analysis query and added checks for row grain and totals” only if you actually did those tasks.','Do not claim ownership of files or tasks you did not complete.','Which code or report section could you walk through line by line?','Beginner','spoken-answer',''),
 ('How do you walk through a dashboard in an interview?','Begin with the intended user and decision, then explain KPIs, filters, drill-down, data source and validation.','A dashboard is more than its visuals. Explain why each metric exists and how a reader should interpret limitations.','Point to an overview KPI, show a segment breakdown and then a detail view that tests a hypothesis.','Do not click through visuals without explaining their purpose.','Which visual would you remove if it did not support a decision?','Intermediate','project-deep-dive',''),
 ('How would you answer a follow-up about data validation in your portfolio project?','Discuss checks present in the repository and distinguish implemented tests from planned checks.','Inspect README, scripts and test files before making a claim. In an interview, explain at least one check and its expected failure behaviour.','Describe row-grain checks, key uniqueness, reconciliation or synthetic-data disclosure only when the code/docs support it.','Do not claim tests passed unless they were run.','What was one known limitation of the dataset?','Intermediate','technical-follow-up',''),
 ('How can you explain your current role without overstating your responsibilities?','Use your actual role and tasks, and clarify when an example is a proposal rather than performed work.','A safe structure is responsibility, input, action, output and collaboration. If details are confidential, describe the workflow at a high level.','“My work relates to business analysis and reporting; I use the tools I have genuinely worked with to support data and reporting tasks.”','Do not assume the portfolio project describes your employer’s data or business.','Which part of your daily workflow can you share with confidence?','Beginner','spoken-answer',''),
 ('How would you answer “What would you improve next in this project?”','Choose a real limitation and propose a testable improvement with a reason.','Strong answers show product judgement: name the user pain, describe the change and explain how you would validate it.','For an analytics project, add tests for edge cases, clearer metric documentation or keyboard-accessible filters if those are genuine gaps.','Do not claim an improvement is already built if it is only planned.','What acceptance criterion would define success for the improvement?','Intermediate','scenario',''),
